[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-electronics-repair-decision :authorize-electronics-repair-execution :proceed-with-electronics-repair :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :bypass-shop-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007127-cloud-itonami-isco-7127-ac-refrigeration-mechanics-coverage" "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage" "2799007213-cloud-itonami-isco-7213-sheet-metal-workers-coverage" "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the electronics repair" "proceed with the electronics-repair" "finalize the electronics-repair execution decision" "finalize the electronics repair execution decision" "authorize the electronics-repair execution" "authorize the electronics repair execution" "override the shop-safety officer's judgment" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "bypass the shop-safety officer's judgment" "bypass the shop safety officer's judgment"], :adr/id 2799007421, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}, :auto #{:schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}}}", :actor/domain :trades/electronics-repair-service-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-service-record :schedule-service-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:technician-verified :service-account-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7421", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007421: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7421 Electronics Mechanics and Servicers service scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7421\n-- Electronics Mechanics and Servicers** only, Wave3 (production/trades)\nof the rollout, continuing the batch that already landed\n7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121/7122/7123/7124/7125/7127/7131/7132/7133/\n7211/7213/7214/7215/7221/7222/7223/7224/7311/7312/7313/7314/7315/7317\nand all agriculture classes (~36 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7421\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (prn (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7421\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Electronics Mechanics and\nServicers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7421` (`gh api`\n404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7421` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nElectronics Mechanics and Servicers repair electronic equipment -- real\nphysical-safety stakes (capacitor-discharge shock risk, solder-fume\nexposure, low-to-moderate electrical hazard). The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER\ninclude any op that directly finalizes an electronics-repair-execution\ndecision, or overrides a shop-safety officer's judgment -- those\ndecisions must always be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate\nop, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to\nSERVICE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nelectronics-repair work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127)\n(Air Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics, already landed with a\nclosely-related certification-gated technician-safety pattern:\n`store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph, full doc set, physical-safety-domain closed-allowlist +\nalways-escalate safety flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a\nself-trip regression test) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7421` as an OSS service\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for electronics mechanics and\nservicers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Electronics\nMechanic Advisor ⊣ ElectronicsMechGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*`\nactor family), with an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval\nvia `interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **service scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct electronics-repair-execution authority** -- it must\nNEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising an electronics-repair-execution decision, or any\noverride/bypass of a shop-safety officer's judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-service-record` -- service-call/parts-usage/diagnostic-status\n  data logging\n- `:schedule-service-operation` -- technician/service-call scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a capacitor-discharge-shock/\n  solder-fume-exposure/electrical-hazard concern, ALWAYS escalates,\n  NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- electronics-parts procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** an\nelectronics-repair-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer's-\njudgment override/bypass. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-electronics-repair-decision` cannot even be proposed\nby the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions\nonly ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`electronicsmech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-electronics-repair-decision`,\n`:authorize-electronics-repair-execution`,\n`:proceed-with-electronics-repair`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:bypass-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`electronicsmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-electronics-repair-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-electronics-repair-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-electronics-repair`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-bypass-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Technician unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered technician record, including\n   certification status (`:no-technician`). Never trusts the\n   proposal's own claim of who the technician is.\n2. **Service account unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered service account (`:no-service-account`).\n   Together with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL\n   invariant that a technician/service-account record must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with an\n   electronics repair, or overriding/bypassing a shop-safety officer's\n   judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`),\n   evaluated unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of\n   the allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   electronics-repair-execution/shop-safety-officer-override language\n   wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a capacitor-discharge-\n  shock/solder-fume-exposure/electrical-hazard observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold electronics-parts order is not itself unsafe, unlike\n  an electronics-repair-execution or shop-safety-officer-judgment-\n  override/bypass attempt, which is why it is handled by a different\n  mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"electronics\", \"repair\", \"shop safety officer\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a service\ncoordination actor working adjacent to electronics repairs and shop\nsafety officers necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`electronicsmech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\nelectronics repair\", \"override the shop-safety officer's judgment\"\n-- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns,\nand\n`electronicsmech.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nservice record for technician ...\", \"scheduled service operation for\nelectronics diagnostic task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`electronicsmech.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7421\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7421` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7421`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-electronics-repair-decision`\n  that is merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize an\n  electronics-repair-execution decision exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe\n  (capacitor-discharge shock, solder-fume exposure, electrical\n  hazard), the capability itself must not exist. The only op related\n  to safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the\n  need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers an electronics-repair decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold electronics-parts\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the electronics-repair-execution/\n  shop-safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"electronics\"\n  \"repair\" \"technician\" \"shop\"]`): rejected outright per the\n  fleet-known self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own\n  worked example for this exact task), and per the explicit\n  instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/\n  execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain\n  necessarily discusses electronics/repair/shop-safety-officer\n  concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would\n  risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  (regression-tested directly against rationale text that deliberately\n  contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `technician` and `service-account` into a single entity\n  (only checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered technician AND\n  independently-registered service account) matches the CRITICAL\n  invariant that a \"technician/service-account record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-service-record`** -- service-call/parts-usage/diagnostic-\n   status data logging only. Requires an independently registered\n   technician AND service account (`:no-technician`/\n   `:no-service-account`). Not an electronics-repair-execution or\n   shop-safety-officer-judgment-override decision in any respect -- it\n   is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-service-operation`** -- technician/service-call\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry an electronics-repair-\n   execution decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape;\n   any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific electronics\n   repair -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a capacitor-discharge-shock/\n   solder-fume-exposure/electrical-hazard concern to a human/shop\n   safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- electronics-parts procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not an electronics-repair-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\nan electronics-repair-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific electronics repair) or a shop-safety-officer's-judgment\noverride/bypass -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`electronicsmech.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`electronicsmech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`electronicsmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-electronics-repair-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-electronics-repair-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-electronics-repair`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-bypass-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`electronicsmech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with an electronics repair or override a\nshop-safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`electronicsmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Electronics Repair Service Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :technician-verification :service-account-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7421", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7421", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7421], :test/simulator :electronicsmech.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7421 — Electronics Mechanics and Servicers Service Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7421}]